WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:16.285
Unit twenty-three: Great Inventions. In this unit, you will talk about important inventions.

4
00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.157
Invention.

5
00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:22.284
Invention means something new that someone has made for the first time.

6
00:00:22.584 --> 00:00:24.375
The phone is a great invention.

7
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:27.390
Your turn. Say: Invention.

8
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.068
Invention.

9
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:33.038
Invent.

10
00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:36.364
Invent means to make something new for the first time.

11
00:00:36.664 --> 00:00:38.153
Who invented the light bulb?

12
00:00:38.853 --> 00:00:41.506
Your turn. Say: Invent.

13
00:00:44.206 --> 00:00:45.137
Invent.

14
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:46.954
Wheel.

15
00:00:47.654 --> 00:00:50.629
Wheel means a round thing that turns and helps things move.

16
00:00:50.929 --> 00:00:52.615
The wheel is very old.

17
00:00:53.315 --> 00:00:56.431
Your turn. Say: Wheel.

18
00:00:59.131 --> 00:00:59.900
Wheel.

19
00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:01.895
Telephone.

20
00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.662
Telephone means a machine for talking to people far away.

21
00:01:05.962 --> 00:01:09.471
The telephone was invented in 1876.

22
00:01:10.171 --> 00:01:12.893
Your turn. Say: Telephone.

23
00:01:15.593 --> 00:01:16.536
Telephone.

24
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.621
Light bulb.

25
00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:22.272
Light bulb means a glass thing that gives electric light.

26
00:01:22.572 --> 00:01:24.351
Change the light bulb, please.

27
00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:28.214
Your turn. Say: Light bulb.

28
00:01:30.914 --> 00:01:31.857
Light bulb.

29
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:33.584
Internet.

30
00:01:34.284 --> 00:01:37.317
Internet means a network that links computers around the world.

31
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:39.431
I use the internet for homework.

32
00:01:40.131 --> 00:01:43.747
Your turn. Say: Internet.

33
00:01:46.447 --> 00:01:47.343
Internet.

34
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.235
Useful.

35
00:01:49.935 --> 00:01:52.213
Useful means helping you to do something.

36
00:01:52.513 --> 00:01:54.315
A dictionary is very useful.

37
00:01:55.015 --> 00:01:57.505
Your turn. Say: Useful.

38
00:02:00.205 --> 00:02:01.218
Useful.

39
00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:03.113
Change.

40
00:02:03.813 --> 00:02:05.441
Change means to make different.

41
00:02:05.741 --> 00:02:07.694
Inventions change our lives.

42
00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.513
Your turn. Say: Change.

43
00:02:13.213 --> 00:02:13.947
Change.

44
00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.066
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:17.366 --> 00:02:20.073
Sreypich, what is the most useful invention?

46
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:23.023
I think it's the internet.

47
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:26.142
When was the telephone invented?

48
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:32.062
It was invented in 1876, by Alexander Graham Bell.

49
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:34.212
And the wheel?

50
00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:37.992
It was invented thousands of years ago!

51
00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:42.235
Grammar focus: Was invented by and in.

52
00:02:42.535 --> 00:02:47.135
The telephone was invented in 1876.

53
00:02:47.435 --> 00:02:49.597
Use 'by' for the person and 'in' for the year.

54
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:53.561
Now read and listen. Ideas That Changed the World.

55
00:02:53.861 --> 00:02:55.663
Inventions change our lives.

56
00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.507
The wheel was invented thousands of years ago.

57
00:03:00.817 --> 00:03:07.077
The telephone was invented in 1876, and the light bulb soon after.

58
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:10.870
The internet changed how we learn, work and talk.

59
00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:14.520
Which invention do you think is the most useful?

60
00:03:15.817 --> 00:03:18.481
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:18.781 --> 00:03:22.545
The telephone was invented blank 1876.

62
00:03:22.845 --> 00:03:25.477
A, in. B, on. C, by.

63
00:03:29.483 --> 00:03:31.274
The answer is A: in.

64
00:03:32.783 --> 00:03:35.212
It was invented blank Alexander Graham Bell.

65
00:03:35.512 --> 00:03:38.376
A, by. B, in. C, at.

66
00:03:42.383 --> 00:03:43.895
The answer is A: by.

67
00:03:45.383 --> 00:03:47.394
Helping you do something means blank.

68
00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.942
A, useful. B, famous. C, old.

69
00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.077
The answer is A: useful.

70
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:02.548
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you think is the most useful invention?

71
00:04:07.848 --> 00:04:13.202
I think the internet is the most useful invention because we can learn anything and talk to people everywhere.

72
00:04:13.502 --> 00:04:15.328
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:16.317 --> 00:04:20.536
Great work today! You learned eight new words and was invented by and in.

74
00:04:20.836 --> 00:04:24.905
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

75
00:04:25.205 --> 00:04:27.985
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

76
00:04:28.285 --> 00:04:31.402
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

